All types of flowmeters share a common
schematic symbol
. While the
symbol itself does not indicate flow direction
, most flowmeters are designed to be read in
only one direction
.
By understanding the
different types of flowmeters and their applications
, technicians can accurately
monitor and diagnose
hydraulic systems, ensuring
optimal performance and reliability
.